cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Logic Drift: An Initial Protocol for Probing Consensus-Validity Separation in Language Models"
message: "If you use this working paper or reproducibility package, please cite it using this metadata."
type: dataset
version: "0.1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Tsakiris
    given-names: Alex
    affiliation: "Future of Inquiry Institute"
    email: alex.futureofinquiry@gmail.com
abstract: "A working paper and reproducibility package introducing the Logic Drift Protocol, a compact evaluation method that asks language models to score a fixed inference from multiple angles (consensus, inductive support, deductive validity, neutral-domain structural twin). Reports initial behavioral results from 697 successful runs across seven frontier models on a single consciousness-related test case, with paired confidence intervals and within-run effect sizes."
keywords:
  - large language models
  - LLM evaluation
  - sycophancy
  - reasoning
  - prompt sensitivity
  - consensus
  - validity
  - philosophy of mind
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/1940alex/logic-drift-protocol"
date-released: "2026-05-17"
